  "facts": [
    "The Hvalfjörður Tunnel, opened on 11 July 1998, stretches 5,770 meters beneath the fjord, plunging 165 meters below sea level at its deepest point.",
    "Built as Iceland's first private finance initiative, the tunnel cost about ISK 5,000 million (USD 70 million) and was designed for 5,000 vehicles daily, yet traffic now exceeds 8,000 vehicles.",
